    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2505.04242v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "Particle-resolved simulations of dense frictional suspensions undergoing the viscous-inertial transition using pressure-imposed rheology. The study varies fluid viscosity, shear rate, and granular pressure, and examines the effect of interparticle friction on the transition. The key findings are the distinct scalings of packing fraction phi and macroscopic friction mu, governed by different alpha values, and the role of tangential contact and lubrication forces.",
